  "notes": "REGISTER:\nThis is a rough, derogatory word. It's often used when the speaker is angry or dismissive of what someone else is saying. Common in confrontational speech and media.\n\nUSAGE:\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ほざく - to spout/babble (something)\n- ほざくな - shut up, stop spouting nonsense\n- ⟦{何|なに}→何：00498_nani⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ほざいて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ - what are you blabbering about\nVery informal and can be considered rude. Mostly heard in fiction, arguments, or when expressing strong irritation.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ほざく - to babble, mouth off (derogatory)\n- ⟦{言|い}う→言う：00515_iu⟧ - to say (neutral)\n- ⟦しゃべる→しゃべる：02117_shaberu⟧ - to talk, chat (casual)\n- ⟦{吠|ほ}える→吠える：02415_hoeru⟧ - to bark, to yell (also derogatory when about speech)",
